<task id="114" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>ISS-024 — an external *licensed* system user is treated the same as an internal one (owner-decided)</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (queued 2026-09-18 by owner directive)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Share write path (.cs, Api/ExternalAccess); tags bff-api/auth; modifies tests. Removes a refusal, i.e. widens who can be granted access.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A localized removal with a clear owner ruling. Unchanged from the stub, and verification supports it: the change is three code sites plus two test sites, all identified. The one judgment point — that the owner's stated discriminator (licence) is not read anywhere in this path — is an escalation trigger rather than open-ended design.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Api/ExternalAccess/** is parallel-unsafe in this project.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>063</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3–4 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Register ISS-024 / GitHub #1003. Found by task 063 (session 13) and raised as an open owner question in every handoff since. Owner decision received 2026-09-18; queued by the same directive. Authored 2026-09-19 with premises re-verified against HEAD — BOTH cited line numbers were wrong and a SECOND test site exists, see `&lt;notes&gt;`.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <owner-decision date="2026-09-18">"For task 063 an 'external' licensed user is treated the same as an internal licensed user." LICENCE, not the external flag, is the discriminator: a licensed system user is a Dataverse security principal and can hold a POA share, whether or not the directory marks them external.</owner-decision>

  <prompt>`POST /api/v1/external-access/share-user` refuses a system user whose `sprk_isexternal` flag is not `false` with HTTP 422 `sdap.access.user_share.user_not_internal`. Per the owner's ruling that refusal goes.

🔴 **The register's two citations are both wrong — use these instead.** The refusal is the third branch of `EligibilityRefusal`, at **`InternalShareEndpoints.cs:677-680`** (`if (user.IsExternal is not false) return Refused(…)`), inside the method at `:666-683`. `InternalShareEndpoints.cs:80` — which the register and the earlier stub both named — is only the reason-code CONSTANT declaration. And `SystemUserIdentityResolver.cs:57` does NOT justify this refusal: that doc comment (`:50-69`) is about internal-only MESSAGE exclusion feeding `CommunicationAccessContext.IsInternalUser` for notification fan-out and the timeline read path. It is a different feature, the share path does not use that resolver, and `sprk_isexternal` REMAINS load-bearing there. Do not touch the resolver or the flag itself.

🔴 **Ship the test with the code, and there are TWO test sites, not one.** `tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/InternalUserShareContractTests.cs:80-95` asserts the 422 and the reason code; `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/InternalUserShareTests.cs:430-441` is a `[Theory]` over `true` and `null` asserting `(422, UserNotInternalReasonCode)`. The register names only the first — a repo grep for the reason-code string misses the second because it asserts through the constant.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external access share path.</role>
  <goal>A licensed system user can be granted a POA share regardless of the external flag; the test suite asserts the new rule rather than the retired one; and no prose left in the code or notes still states the retired rule.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 063 built the internal share routes. Eligibility is decided by `EligibilityRefusal` (`InternalShareEndpoints.cs:666-683`) in three branches, in order: disabled (`:668-670`), not-a-person — an application id or an access mode outside 0–2 (`:672-675`) — and not-internal (`:677-680`). Only the third is retired. The first two are what actually keep a non-principal out, and they must keep working.

**The `null` case is a real decision, not a detail.** The branch is `user.IsExternal is not false`, so an UNREADABLE or absent flag currently refuses — the ADR-003 fail-closed posture, and `InternalUserShareTests.cs:432` pins it with an explicit `[InlineData(null)]`. Deleting the branch makes `null` PASS. That is the correct consequence of the ruling (the flag becomes irrelevant to this decision), but it removes a fail-closed guard and must be stated deliberately rather than absorbed.

**What `sprk_isexternal` is, answered from code so it need not be guessed.** It is Spaarke's own custom two-option column on `systemuser` (`SystemUserIdentityResolver.cs:82`, `InternalShareEndpoints.cs:744-746`), default 'No'/internal, read fail-closed to external when missing. It is NOT an AAD/directory guest marker. It is consumed by the communication fan-out to exclude external licensed users from internal-only content — pinned live at `tests/integration/seam/Communication/FanOutTargetingSecuritySeamTests.cs:249-255`. So the flag stays; only this path's use of it goes.

**The discriminator the owner names is not read here.** `SystemUserSelect` (`:117`) is `systemuserid,isdisabled,accessmode,applicationid,sprk_isexternal` — no licence column, and a repo-wide search for `islicensed`/`caltype` finds nothing in `src/**` (one comment in `scripts/debug/list-app-users.ps1:24`). After the branch goes, eligibility is "exists, enabled, is a person", which is a PROXY for "licensed security principal", not a licence check. See the escalation.

Contract check, already done: no client consumes the reason code — a search of `src/client/**` for `user_not_internal` returns nothing. Only the two tests reference it.

Fixture note for the test edits: the fake systemuser table VALIDATES `$select` against a column allow-list and throws on an unknown column (`InternalUserShareTests.cs:893-900`, list at `:844`), and projects `IsExternal` only when selected (`:918`). Selecting FEWER columns is safe.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InternalShareEndpoints.cs (the refusal branch :677-680; the reason-code constant :79-80; `SystemUserSelect` :117; the class doc prose :44-48; `SystemUserRow.IsExternal` :744-746)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/InternalUserShareContractTests.cs (the 422 contract test :79-95; the `SystemUserRow` helper :156-157)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/InternalUserShareTests.cs (the [Theory] :430-441)</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-063-internal-user-share-endpoints.md (the reason-code list :133; the prose claim :355)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Identity/SystemUserIdentityResolver.cs:50-69 (what `sprk_isexternal` is FOR — a different feature; read it, do NOT change it)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Communication/FanOutTargetingSecuritySeamTests.cs:249-255 (the flag's live consumer, which must stay green)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="audit 2026-09-18">Scope: the commit. 🔴 SHIP THE TESTS WITH THE CODE, in ONE commit, and there are TWO test sites (`InternalUserShareContractTests.cs:80-95` and `InternalUserShareTests.cs:430-441`). A green suite after changing only the endpoint would mean the tests never exercised the path; a green suite after changing only a test would mean nothing at all.</constraint>
    <constraint source="verified 2026-09-19">Scope: the flag. `sprk_isexternal` and `ISystemUserIdentityResolver.IsExternalAsync` MUST NOT be removed, renamed or repurposed. They are the authoritative internal-vs-external source for internal-only communication exclusion, pinned by the Communication seam tests. This task removes ONE consumer of the flag, not the flag.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md fact 4">Scope: the subject. ⚠️ A *contact* is still NOT a security principal: it cannot be a POA share target and cannot be impersonated (`projects/unified-access-control-r2/CLAUDE.md:23`). This decision covers licensed SYSTEM USERS only, and the contact plane must keep COMPUTING access rather than storing it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 063">Scope: rights vocabulary. The share write path's rights vocabulary is Dataverse's, not Spaarke's — the two have same-named values with different bit layouts (Spaarke Delete = 4; Dataverse 4 = Append). Assert Dataverse's numbers as literals rather than deriving them from the table under test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the response contract. Removing a reasonCode is a contract change. No client consumes `user_not_internal` (verified — nothing in `src/client/**`), so state the change explicitly and decide deliberately whether the constant is deleted or retained as unused; do not leave a dead refusal path that can still be reached.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: the remaining guards. The disabled and not-a-person refusals stay, and both keep failing closed on an unreadable value. Only the external branch is retired — a user who cannot be confirmed to EXIST, or who is an application/support/delegated-admin account, is still refused.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: prose. Every sentence stating the retired rule must change in the same commit — the class doc (`:44-48`), the constant's summary (`:79`) if retained, and the task-063 notes (`:133`, `:355`). A file that reads consistently and describes the wrong rule is this project's signature failure mode.</constraint>
  </constraints>

